# Optional integrations for MyNews.
#
# Every key here is OPTIONAL. A source whose credentials are missing is
# skipped, not failed — the feed keeps working and GET /api/health reports it
# under "skippedSources" with the reason. So you can commit the full source
# list and switch integrations on one at a time.
#
# Copy this file to .env (or set the variables in your host's environment).
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
#
# GNews — global news index, 80,000+ sources in 41 languages.
#
#   Register:  https://gnews.io/register
#   Pricing:   https://gnews.io/pricing
#   Docs:      https://docs.gnews.io/
#
# Free tier: 100 requests/day, 1 request/second, 10 articles per request, and
# a 12-hour delay on the data. Because the quota is per DAY, the GNews sources
# are cached for 3 hours (ttlMinutes: 180 in feeds.js) — eight sources then
# cost ~64 requests/day rather than the ~2,300 a 5-minute cache would cost.
# Used for: markets, business, crypto, cyber, politics, space, health.
# The key is passed as ?apikey=<key>.
GNEWS_KEY=

# ── The 4 other wired into feeds.js ───────────────────────────────────────
# The Guardian Open Platform — deep, sectioned coverage.
# Used for: ai, business, investments, markets, macro, cyber, gaming, politics.
#
#   Register (free, non-commercial):
#     https://bonobo.capi.gutools.co.uk/register/developer
#   Landing page:
#     https://open-platform.theguardian.com/access
#   Docs:
#     https://open-platform.theguardian.com/documentation
#
# The key arrives immediately after the form. It is passed as ?api-key=<key>.
# The free tier is for NON-COMMERCIAL use and is rate limited — if MyNews ever
# earns money, request a commercial key at the /register/commercial page.
GUARDIAN_KEY=

# NewsAPI — broad multi-publisher headlines.
# Used for: ai, business, markets.
#
#   Register:  https://newsapi.org/register
#   Docs:      https://newsapi.org/docs/get-started
#
# Free developer tier is 100 requests/day and requires visible attribution
# back to the publisher. The key is passed as ?apiKey=<key>.
NEWSAPI_KEY=

# TMDB — film, TV and anime discovery.
# Used for: film-tv, marvel-dc, manga-anime.
#
#   Sign in, then:  https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
#
# Click "Create New API Key", fill in an application name and description.
# The key is passed as ?api_key=<key>.
TMDB_KEY=

# Twelve Data — live FX and market quotes.
# Used for: fx-rates, investments.
#
#   Register:  https://twelvedata.com/register
#   Pricing:   https://twelvedata.com/pricing
#
# Free tier gives 800 requests/day and 8 API credits per request. The key is
# passed as ?apikey=<key>.
TWELVEDATA_KEY=

# Reddit OAuth2 — subreddit depth.
# Used for: gaming, film-tv, marvel-dc, sneakers, watches, armenia.
#
#   Log in to Reddit first, then:  https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps
#   Or the developer portal:      https://developers.reddit.com/apps/
#
# Create a "script" app. The redirect URI can be anything, e.g.
# http://localhost:8080 — this app uses the client-credentials flow and never
# follows the redirect. Reddit's public .json endpoints answer 403 without
# OAuth, which is why the API is used here rather than RSS.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Next tier — not wired up yet, but same pattern when you want them ─────
#
#   Alpha Vantage (stocks, forex, commodities)  https://www.alphavantage.co/support/
#   Finnhub (60 req/min, forex + company news)  https://finnhub.io/register
#   SerpApi (Google News results, 100/mo free)  https://serpapi.com/users/sign_up
#   NewsData.io (news, free tier)               https://newsdata.io/register
#   Currents API (news, 500/day free)           https://currentsapi.services/en/register
#   Brave Search API (web + news search)        https://brave.com/search/api/
#   GNews.io (news, free tier)                  https://gnews.io/register
#   Marketstack (stock data, free tier)         https://marketstack.com/signup
#   ContextualWeb (web search, free tier)       https://contextualweb.com/register
#   Massive, formerly Polygon.io (stocks)       https://massive.com/dashboard/signup
#
# ── Keyless, no configuration needed ──────────────────────────────────────
# These are already wired up and need nothing from you:
#   arXiv, OpenAlex, Open Library, DEV Community, Stack Exchange,
#   Hacker News (Algolia), Frankfurter (FX), CoinGecko, Google News,
#   Wikipedia, World Bank, FRED CSV, BLS public API, Eurostat.
